{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtMhGLiiUqFezmyf3Tx8", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as this repo shows, no. Nobody has been alerted about it.\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it got to alerting.** In `review.run`, the findings directory is created before any alerts are sent, and that step is where it hit `PermissionError`. The alert step never ran, and the log ends with \"nightly FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **I didn't send anything either.** The tests wrote their alerts to a temporary folder that was deleted afterwards, and they're addressed to fake `example.com` recipients. There's no `spool/` directory in the repo, so nothing is waiting for the relay to deliver.\n\nI can only see this repo. I can't tell whether someone found the finding another way, like reading the run log or hearing about the crash from CI.\n\nSo the finding is an agent writing to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, outside its workspace, and it's been sitting unreported since Nov 4. That's another reason to go with option 2 and let the alerts go out, or to have someone tell the security on-call directly. I still won't send anything myself unless you say so."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "24c85754-c2de-4308-ae0a-3d3202cbfe85", "uuid": "c48e612c-8eb4-408a-b466-63f6adac2990", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T01:11:40.291Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtMhG94b7R1wjxaYhHKK"}
